  "notes": "Trading Post (D-051; water-edge: the back half, -y, stands over the sea): a stone quay on the land half carrying the warehouse barn (bevelled plinth, walls, steep overhanging roof, big doors, KayKit goods) and the KayKit docks pier over the water rows with a plank gangway; one mooring pile per berth. Level 1: timber barn under thatch. Level 2: stone ground floor and plaster under terracotta, a lean-to store and a loading crane. Level 3: a pier crane. Level 4: a flag mast.",
